body.body:
Thanks for testing.

@mehturt are you sure this is from NC? Turning on/off screen should not affect our app as we just go for a timeout (10s).

@joekerna we are using the built-in device credentials screen, which varies from device to device. On some there is only a very little fingerprint icon on the bottom.
Can you maybe post a screenshot? (Unfortunately you will have to take a picture with a different phone as screenshots are prohibited when device lock is enabled)

But all in all it seems to be better :+1:

True, the file to be uploaded is first copied in internal storage and then uploaded.
I am unsure for the reason, but I think it might be so that the file cannot be removed (e.g. external storage removed) while uploading.

@ezaquarii @AndyScherzinger I think we can change this, or?

@AndyScherzinger exactly. Already uploaded files would have to be moved by the user if they want so.

However if you really want to reupload everything, you should be able to simply delete the auto upload folder config and recreate it (maybe you can try to disable/re-enable first, but I have never tested that).

edit: @tleydxdy I think this solution would also work for you

@AndyScherzinger It has been fixed and tested on my own ("par mes soins" in french 🇫🇷 😄 ) in : https://github.com/nextcloud/android/pull/5465

I let you watch the PR

Have a nice day
